./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:2:[[A]] [[OBJ:three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0]] [[SEM:ralph_claude_code_autoresearch_as_line_formation_mirrors]]
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:12:- reread the three reference folders again
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:14:- then reread our own space with that lens
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:46:  - `plugins/hookify/core/rule_engine.py`
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:65:Ralph forms a line very early by **shrinking the work surface** and **externalizing carry-over memory**.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:96:Claude Code main forms a line early by **turning behaviors into surfaces and hooks**.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:101:- packaged
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:116:**repeated behavior -> named intervention rule -> surface packaging -> workflow layer**
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:121:Claude Code forces line formation through surface and intervention points.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:127:- a hook-based correction surface
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:129:It is weaker when line meaning should remain latent for longer before surface packaging.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:135:autoresearch forms a line early by **fixing the experiment harness** and **narrowing the mutable surface**.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:148:**fixed harness -> narrow mutable surface -> experiment -> keep/discard pressure**
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:180:- package behaviors into visible surfaces
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:183:- shape workflow through surface instrumentation
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:188:- narrow the mutable surface
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:208:- reread before fixation
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:210:- user-language meaning reread before final surface truth
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:215:**material intake -> hold/calibration -> repeated reread -> meaning thickening -> later condensation**
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:225:- Claude Code exposes that our space still lacks later-stage hook/surface packaging for matured lines
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:226:- autoresearch exposes that our space still lacks later-stage bounded mutable surfaces and comparability rails
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:231:- our space tolerates latent meaning longer than Claude Code surface packaging
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:244:These rereads make one thing more explicit.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:256:- relation reread
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:267:- Claude Code: delayed plugin/hook/agent surface
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:278:Ralph, Claude Code, and autoresearch all know how to make a line show itself quickly, but they each do it by sacrificing a different kind of openness. Ralph sacrifices ambiguity by cutting the task down until it can be closed. Claude Code sacrifices latency by surfacing patterns early as commands, hooks, and packaged behavior. autoresearch sacrifices ambiguity even harder by locking the experiment frame and asking one narrow mutable surface to prove itself against a hard metric.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:280:Our space has been doing something else. It has been letting the material stay alive longer before deciding what it is. It keeps weak possibilities around, rereads them through different layers, and only later lets them thicken into something that can become a reusable operator, a visible surface, or a bounded execution rail. That is why the space often looks slower or less decisive on the outside. But what these three references make visible is that this slowness is not emptiness. It is a different line formation rhythm.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:282:So the important insight is not that we need to become Ralph, Claude Code, or autoresearch. The insight is that once our own lines have thickened enough, we can finally see what those references really are: not competing cores, but attachable parts for later. Ralph can become an execution memory rail. Claude Code can become a pluginized intervention surface. autoresearch can become a bounded experiment harness. They are useful precisely because they are not our foundation.
./docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:296:**our space is already good at keeping lines alive long enough to thicken, but it is still weak at later-stage packaging of matured lines into execution rails, hook surfaces, and bounded mutable experiment lanes.**
./references/vectorfl_next/docs/decisions/FIRST_SCALE_REVIEW_POLICY.md:5:The first scale review is a descriptive pass over the current widened runtime. It does not introduce new core states, new ontology, or pass/fail gates. It rereads the current field through the five agreed review axes:
./references/vectorfl_next/docs/decisions/FIRST_SCALE_REVIEW_POLICY.md:11:- non-purpose survival
./references/vectorfl_next/docs/decisions/FIRST_SCALE_REVIEW_POLICY.md:23:First-scale expansion is no longer a tiny bootstrap. The engine now needs a recurring review pass that checks whether wider space still preserves quiet presence, varied formation speeds, reflux material, observer consistency, and non-purpose survival.
